.IX Title "Clownfish::Class 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Class 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Class \- Class.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $class = Clownfish::Class\->fetch_class(\*(AqFoo::Bar\*(Aq);
\&    my $subclass = Clownfish::Class\->singleton(\*(AqFoo::Bar::Jr\*(Aq, $class);
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Classes are first-class objects in Clownfish.  Class objects are instances
of Clownfish::Class.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS fetch_class
.IX Subsection "fetch_class"
.Vb 1
\&    my $class = Clownfish::Class\->fetch_class($class_name);
.Ve
.PP
Find a registered class.  May return undef if the class is not
registered.
.SS singleton
.IX Subsection "singleton"
.Vb 4
\&    my $class = Clownfish::Class\->singleton(
\&        class_name => $class_name,  # required
\&        parent     => $parent,      # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a singleton.  If a Class can be found in the registry based on
the supplied class name, it will be returned.  Otherwise, a new Class
will be created using \f(CW\*(C`parent\*(C'\fR as a base.
.PP
If \f(CW\*(C`parent\*(C'\fR is undef, an attempt will be made to find it.  If the
attempt fails, an error will result.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS make_obj
.IX Subsection "make_obj"
.Vb 1
\&    my $obj = $class\->make_obj();
.Ve
.PP
Create an empty object of the type defined by the Class: allocate,
assign its class and give it an initial refcount of 1.  The caller is
responsible for initialization.
.SS get_name
.IX Subsection "get_name"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $class\->get_name();
.Ve
.PP
Return the name of the class.
.SS get_parent
.IX Subsection "get_parent"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $class\->get_parent();
.Ve
.PP
Return the parent class, or undef for a root of the class
hierarchy.
.SS get_obj_alloc_size
.IX Subsection "get_obj_alloc_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $class\->get_obj_alloc_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of bytes needed to hold an instance of the class.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Class isa Clownfish::Obj.
